From 18afb07c6d41fa811d75c0386996ae76cc783993 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lmoresi <louis.moresi@anu.edu.au>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 22:51:37 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] A fill ring that touches itself is refused; one name for the
 seam-conforming path's refusals

A cavity ring with a vertex on one of its own non-adjacent edges (a touch,
not a proper crossing, so the crossing count is 0) hung gmsh: two outcrop
placements with a rail point projected onto the wall built such rings at
1e-15 of the edge, and no gmsh option (algorithm, retries, abort on error)
turned the spin into an error. _refuse_a_ring_touching_itself refuses a
ring whose vertex lies within 1e-9 of the local edge length of a
non-adjacent edge, naming the vertex and the edge, inside the gathered
tries of the three 2-D fills. Rings of placements that complete come no
closer than 1.8e-2.

Also, from the reviews of the previous commit:
- every refusal on the seam-conforming path starts 'seam-conforming path:',
  set once where _place_thin_volume_2d raises its gathered failures, so the
  connector refusal no longer breaks test_0904's parallel assertion;
- _loop_self_crossings and the ring/hole inside test are vectorised
  (n = 1000: 2.3 s to 0.03 s; all three guards 0.15 s), with the same rule
  (400 random polygons agree);
- _inside_polygon's on-edge band is 1e-12 of the polygon's diameter, not an
  absolute 1e-14, and the connector's touch test is relative too;
- the band guard names its remedy, seams='gather'.

Tests (test_0909): both dumped rings refused; the vertex moved 1e-6 and
1e-2 inside passes, 1e-12 refused; the closest completing ring passes; each
guard reached through place_fault_ribbon_2d (a spy); the inside test and
the connector's touch test at scales 1 and 1e-6. Shown to fail on:
threshold 0, threshold 2e-2, each call site removed, the old on-edge band,
the old connector tolerance.

Underworld development team with AI support from Claude Code
